---
profile: moderate

exclude_paths:
  - .github/
  - reports/
  - .ansible_facts/
  # The vendored Postal fork. Its YAML is a Rails application's, not Ansible's.
  - vendor/
  # Downloaded collections. The lint job installs them one step before running this.
  - collections/

skip_list:
  # var-naming[no-role-prefix] fires 113 times, on every role in the project, and the
  # convention it asks for is the wrong one here. Roles in this bench PUBLISH facts that
  # other plays consume — postal_seed is read by benchmark.yml and reset.yml,
  # postal_image_resolved by the compose template and the report — because a role default is
  # out of scope in any play that does not include that role (see group_vars/all/15-paths.yml).
  # Those names are cross-role contracts, and prefixing them per role would be misleading.
  # The genuinely role-local registers among the 113 could be renamed, but that is a
  # mechanical change across every role with a real chance of missing a reference, and it
  # buys nothing today. Noted in roadmap.md.
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
  # Test-bench roles are only ever launched by their own playbooks, so they
  # do not need Galaxy metadata.
  - meta-no-info
  # Lifecycle playbooks (reset, benchmark, calibrate) are non-idempotent
  # by design: the comparison protocol requires an identical starting state
  # before every run.
  - no-changed-when

warn_list:
  - experimental
  - command-instead-of-module
